{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532565-could-you-survive-being-a-vampire","id":1532565,"title":"Could you survive being a Vampire?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-14T05:56:36-07:00","id":1532565,"title":"Could you survive being a Vampire?","content":"How hard is it to survive World of Darkness and a newly embrace Vampire? I think it would be pretty hard, the sun is now your death sentence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T06:05:21-07:00","id":1532566,"title":"","content":"It really depends how you're Embraced. Just some random caitiff Embraced and dropped into the World of Darkness with absolutely no knowledge or understanding of your condition? Yeah, good luck. Or maybe you wake up as a Sabbat Shovelhead and you're strapped with a couple of grenades, Dominated and pointed towards a Camarilla Justicar? You'll need more than luck just to survive thirty minutes. <br /> <br /> But if you have an more typical Embrace, where your Sire actually takes time to teach you and train you, and you're welcomed into the local Camarilla, I don't think it would be too difficult to survive or even thrive. And some clans would help, like being a Nosferatu would suck. But they really look after their own, so I don't see why it would be very difficult to get by with your night-to-night survival, at least for a decent while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T06:08:51-07:00","id":1532567,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ll let Mr Bulsara and friends answer that one for me:-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=_Jtpf8N5IDE&amp;pp=ygUZV2hvIHdhbnRzIHRvIGxpdmUgZm9yZXZlcg%3D%3D\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=_Jtpf8N5IDE&amp;pp=ygUZV2hvIHdhbnRzIHRvIGxpdmUgZm9yZXZlcg%3D%3D\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=_Jtpf8N5IDE&amp;pp=ygUZV2hvIHdhbnRzIHRvIGxpdmUgZm9yZXZlcg%3D%3D\" target=\"_blank\"> https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=_Jtpf8N5IDE&amp;pp=ygUZV2hvIHdhbnRzIHRvIGxpdmUgZm9yZXZlcg%3D%3D </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T10:19:22-07:00","id":1532582,"title":"","content":"If I was embraced as a shovelhead or Caitiff/Thin blood then honestly I don't give myself good odds reaching even older neonate status. But if I was embraced and I had a decent mentor then I think I would make it past the century mark.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T10:23:31-07:00","id":1532584,"title":"","content":"I have poor people skills, bad judgement of character and even worse skill or perception for social games and goings on. I would most likely die as an outcast and very quickly.<br /> <br /> I feel for my poor Sire who would have wasted a boon, favor or something on Embracing me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T13:23:34-07:00","id":1532604,"title":"","content":"The issue with asking how hard it is to survive revolves around how &quot;realistic&quot; you run the setting. The reality is that most characters players love to make wouldn't survive more than decade at most, let alone centuries or millennia.<br /> <br /> Most clans have criteria for embraces, especially if you have to trade favors with the local prince for the right to do it. Thus, you won't bother with someone pretty or random, but someone who has skills or what equates to Backgrounds that would be immediately useful for you as the sire. At the very least the potential childer would need certain traits just have the potential to survive to be of use. To put it another way, we as players see our characters as RPG protagonists, but the sires see our characters as RTS hero characters that they have to expend resources/requisition points to get. Why bother to do it if the unit doesn't do anything?<br /> <br /> This is then stacked on top of the individual clan or bloodline ideology which places value on certain traits, such as the Tremere favoring magical mortals, the Gangrel wanting survivors, or the Giovanni wanting family members, just to name a few. Then you get the faction related issues such as the Camarilla favoring the path of humanity, while the Sabbat prefer loads of violence, and the independents tend to lack allies.<br /> <br /> Can it be relatively easy to survive as a vampire, absolutely it can, but you need to be a specific type of person to do so.<ul><li>Psychologically you can't be co-dependent or desire drama to feel fulfilled.</li> <li>You must be comfortable being alone or isolated for long periods of time.</li> <li>You should have the self-discipline to train in martial arts or maintain a regular gym routine.</li> <li>Mentally you need to hunger for knowledge and be adaptable when change happens.</li> <li>As a mortal you should have an income that is either passive (being a landlord) or can be done from home (stockmarket/programmer/etc).</li> <li>Be the sort who has backup plans for everything.</li> </ul>From there it is just a question of which clan and faction you get embraced by.<br /> <br /> So with that sort of a character baseline, find the most defensible haven location, use your Resources to upgrade it, get a live in Herd so you don't have to bother with hunting, conduct all your vampire related business by phone or video call since Dominate and Presence don't tend to work over technology. From there it is just a question of how you grow your own personal power to catch up to the level of your local kindred.<br /> <br /> Now will this make for a dynamic and interesting character to play, no, no it won't. But it will survive most upheavals because you are not out and about to get caught in the crossfire and your isolation means you are not important enough to prioritize killing, but due to your defense focused havens and backup plans you are seen as too much trouble to try to dig out for next to no gain.<br /> <br /> Or to put it in simpler terms, psychologically you are an INTJ on the MBTI, get embraced by the Tremere, move your haven to a decomissioned missile silo/military bunker which has been converted to a luxury doomsday condo with warding, and slowly build boons with the local kindred by using Dominate to clean up masquerade breaches without having to bother the sheriff or the prince.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":727,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","user":"Thoth","date":". 03-14-2024, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T14:12:36-07:00","id":1532608,"title":"","content":"Myself I wouldn't be noticed by the high clans and many personality quizzes I took show that the Malkavian, Ministry and Ravnos clans would be more willing to consider me. That said I remember Anne Rice Vampire stories and how most don't make it past the first two centuries as the weight of time becomes unbearable and or older vampires might be getting rid of them as we don't want potential rivals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 03-14-2024, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T15:08:10-07:00","id":1532614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532565-could-you-survive-being-a-vampire?p=1532584#post1532584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have poor people skills, bad judgement of character and even worse skill or perception for social games and goings on. I would most likely die as an outcast and very quickly.<br /> <br /> I feel for my poor Sire who would have wasted a boon, favor or something on Embracing me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Either that or you\u2019d live forever because absolutely nobody sees you as a threat! (That approach definately worked for the Emperor Claudius, just ask Sir Derek Jacobi).<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T15:23:15-07:00","id":1532616,"title":"","content":"If you really want a benchmark for how hard it is to survive in WoD as a vampire, run a &quot;play yourself&quot; game.<br /> <br /> Character generation works by comparing yourself to each attribute and skill ranking, then rounding down to account for ego, so if you can lift 300 lbs you have three dots in strength. Go through each stat and Background with the people you will be playing with, it can be surprising how many times your friends will see you as having higher stats than you think you do. Then you just play it out as a situational embrace, so that the clan/bloodline and generation are randomized. The discipline spread is theoretically also randomized, but I find that the ST might want to allocate them so that the coterie has some functionality, i.e. whoever has Dominate as a clan discipline has all three dots in it. <br /> <br /> This approach grounds the character behavior because you can't separate yourself from your character. You know exactly what your character knows, you will destroy your family life if you start beating whoever annoys you, bodies can be annoying to hide or make disappear, etc. That and the Brujah clan weaknesses becomes one of the worst in the game when you are rolling to not eviscerate your younger siblings.<br /> <br /> In a &quot;play yourself&quot; game, just surviving 6 months trying to stabilize your new nocturnal life, figure out how to consistently feed, and how to keep people who knew you from getting involved, is a nightmare. Forget about getting caught up in the local vampire politics, surviving a Sabbat incursion, or tripping over a werewolf den.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T17:52:37-07:00","id":1532625,"title":"","content":"Do I get beginning character stats? Because you pretty much start out as either an olympic athlete, a top level politician/grifter, or a genius. If I'm using my real-life stats...not so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T20:00:03-07:00","id":1532632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532565-could-you-survive-being-a-vampire?p=1532625#post1532625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do I get beginning character stats? Because you pretty much start out as either an olympic athlete, a top level politician/grifter, or a genius. If I'm using my real-life stats...not so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Character stats are a lot like bullet caliber. Everyone loves talking about the big numbers which can blow a hole through anything, yet the humble 22 is often preferred for assassinations or guard suppression due to it being naturally sub-sonic and staying inside the body rather than exiting it. In other words, the stats are not as important as how you use them.<br /> <br /> For example, playing poker isn't particularly complicated which means you don't need Int 5 to play, but if you can use Auspex 1 to see the card reflections in your opponent's eyes, you already know what everyone has, which means you control the game. This can make for a great power dynamic scene in a game, but it can also explain where your character gets Resources 4 from that can't be traced or easily interrupted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T11:57:19-07:00","id":1532709,"title":"","content":"One dot of Celerity, Fortitude, Obsfucate and Presence can easily make the difference of getting out of trouble and living for another night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-20T17:35:33-07:00","id":1532929,"title":"","content":"Um, you can't embrace a werewolf. <br /> <br /> Considering I'm up at dawn, and I dislike being up late, I probably would get really depressed. But I would have more time to read!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532565-could-you-survive-being-a-vampire#post1532565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . . I think it would be pretty hard, the sun is now your death sentence.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the greatest problem right there. We've played other vampire game-systems, like Night's Edge (far more lethal than V:tM, or even CoD: Requiem's new humanity vs. sunlight rules). Having to hide yourself in a place that gets zero sunlight is very difficult.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-20T18:35:14-07:00","id":1532931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532565-could-you-survive-being-a-vampire?p=1532929#post1532929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um, you can't embrace a werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can attempt to embrace them, they just usually die from it. From the vampire point of view, you either get a uniquely powerful ally or you get rid of a potential enemy. Win win.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532565-could-you-survive-being-a-vampire?p=1532929#post1532929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having to hide yourself in a place that gets zero sunlight is very difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so?<br /> <br /> There are two main concerns, one is light safety, the other is enemy safety. Light safety only requires something like a body bag or coffin/large box. Enemy safety just requires your bag or box to be in the attic, basement, closet, or crawl space, preferably disguised as something else.<br /> <br /> One of the best things to do is to have an ornate coffin in the basement rigged with claymores or IEDs so if anyone opens the lid the room gets shredded, while your actual sleeping space is in the attic. Alternatively, if you don't want to bother the neighbors with explosions, then just rig a steel plate door to the basement room with the coffin so that opening the coffin lid makes the door close and lock tight, at which point the halon fire suppression system goes off and displaces all the oxygen in the room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-24T18:32:23-07:00","id":1533101,"title":"","content":"Give me starting stats and clan of choice, I would be fine. Dominate 3, and backgrounds go a long way if the goal is to stay safe while you grow older and stronger. I imagine it would take at least many decades/a century before you got bored enough to feel you had to put yourself in danger by hanging out with other vampires.<br /> <br /> If it was me personally turned into a vampire with a need to operate in daylight right now, I suppose the first thing I would do is offer a life long friend immortality who is in a good position to cut ties (no kids, parents probably gone in a decade or 2 at most since we are in our 50s, parents late 70s to mid 80s) in exchange for daylight services. The next ghoul would be the one who could provide me with the resources I would want to really secure myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-24T18:34:46-07:00","id":1533102,"title":"","content":"By definition, no, I could not survive being a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-24T19:45:17-07:00","id":1533105,"title":"","content":"I think most players and I would last a month at best, unless you have a mentor willing to protect and train you, but there's a 90% chance it's more work than it's worth and even If that weren't the case, I believe I would go crazy in a decade and destroy myself, I don't see myself having hope or anything that motivates me to move forward in this state and I'm not even considering clan curses. Malkavian would be a headache, Lasombra who can't even use a cell phone properly in today's world would be problematic, Ravnos who can't sit still, Nosferatu who would have to live in the sewers if doesn't lose his mind with the transformation. Anyway, the game is cool because it's a game, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T06:07:00-07:00","id":1533120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532565-could-you-survive-being-a-vampire?p=1533105#post1533105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think most players and I would last a month at best</div> </div> </div> </div>Most Players: &quot;I want to play as something different so I can explore and have fun&quot;<br /> Many Players: &quot;The genre and style of the game resonates with my emotional state&quot;<br /> Some Players: &quot;I can finally live out my 1980s action movie fantasy&quot;<br /> A Few Players: &quot;Other than the blood diet and the Beast, it's Tuesday&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":727,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","user":"Thoth","date":". 03-25-2024, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T08:57:43-07:00","id":1533125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532565-could-you-survive-being-a-vampire?p=1533120#post1533120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most Players: &quot;I want to play as something different so I can explore and have fun&quot;<br /> Many Players: &quot;The genre and style of the game resonates with my emotional state&quot;<br /> Sum Players: &quot;I can finally live out my 1980s action movie fantasy&quot;<br /> A Few Players: &quot;Other than the blood diet and the Beast, it's Tuesday&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand if you are following up on my post or sarcastically laughing in my face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T13:59:46-07:00","id":1533135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532565-could-you-survive-being-a-vampire?p=1533125#post1533125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand if you are following up on my post or sarcastically laughing in my face.</div> </div> </div> </div>Following up, though I do find it amusing how many gaming groups I have played in that had the well-behaved sociopath model of the &quot;few players&quot; as the norm, rather than just exploring or playing for fun. STing for a group like that means the baseline of what someone could do or could mentally/emotionally deal with is on a completely different scale than other groups.<br /> <br /> Imagine the following group/coterie:<br /> Nagaraja played by the Mads Mikkelsen version of Hannibal Lector<br /> True Brujah played by MCU Thanos<br /> Giovanni played by Edward Nortons character from the Illusionist<br /> <br /> Now try to sell them on the idea that they feel guilty about feeding on other sentient beings or have to lie to everyone around them to hide their vampiric condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T14:30:02-07:00","id":1533139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532565-could-you-survive-being-a-vampire?p=1533135#post1533135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Following up, though I do find it amusing how many gaming groups I have played in that had the well-behaved sociopath model of the &quot;few players&quot; as the norm, rather than just exploring or playing for fun. STing for a group like that means the baseline of what someone could do or could mentally/emotionally deal with is on a completely different scale than other groups.<br /> <br /> Imagine the following group/coterie:<br /> Nagaraja played by the Mads Mikkelsen version of Hannibal Lector<br /> True Brujah played by MCU Thanos<br /> Giovanni played by Edward Nortons character from the Illusionist<br /> <br /> Now try to sell them on the idea that they feel guilty about feeding on other sentient beings or have to lie to everyone around them to hide their vampiric condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this case it's my fault for lacking details, I wasn't referring to the emotional aspect, human beings are incredibly capable of adapting to a lot of things, however the plots that the kindred participate in and survival at night with hunters and other monsters lurking, I don't think most players wouldn't be adaptable enough to survive this without help or have an important position to be worth protecting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T12:08:03-07:00","id":1533182,"title":"","content":"Unless you have a sire that is willing to mentor on what is okay and not okay in undead society and what do you have that makes you a candiate for the embrace, I can't see many of us being selected for an embrace or enduring past a century or two at best. Sure you could be chosen because you remind them of a lost love or relation and they go ahead with that, but I think that is pretty rare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-04T16:49:00-07:00","id":1533582,"title":"","content":"Some of my players wouldn't survive as vampires; a few have god-complexes: they've literally slaughtered whole shifts of police-officers to the point there's a nation-wide APB after them. In Dark Ages, they even tried that with the town's watch; they gave the hue and cry and, yeah, they got a few mortals, but they eventually got beheaded before midnight. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532565-could-you-survive-being-a-vampire?p=1532931#post1532931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> . . .<br /> <br /> <br /> How so?<br /> <br /> There are two main concerns, one is light safety, the other is enemy safety. Light safety only requires something like a body bag or coffin/large box. Enemy safety just requires your bag or box to be in the attic, basement, closet, or crawl space, preferably disguised as something else.<br /> <br /> One of the best things to do is to have an ornate coffin in the basement rigged with claymores or IEDs so if anyone opens the lid the room gets shredded, while your actual sleeping space is in the attic. Alternatively, if you don't want to bother the neighbors with explosions, then just rig a steel plate door to the basement room with the coffin so that opening the coffin lid makes the door close and lock tight, at which point the halon fire suppression system goes off and displaces all the oxygen in the room.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not as easy as it sounds; boxes and body-bags can have holes that let light in. You can't be to paranoid enough; if some sunlight gets in, just a little, you could be at final-death before you even woke up. <br /> <br /> Claymores and IEDs are a bad idea; for one, that draws attention of mortals. If you want to wake up one evening with a bunch of firefighters and detectives examining your body, yeah. <br /> <br /> The best way is make a haven mortal-proof is have it in a cemetery or, I took this straight from Ann Rice, is, invest in Potence and get a stone so heavy, no mortal could lift it. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-04T17:25:04-07:00","id":1533585,"title":"","content":"Or learn enough Protean and sleep in the ground or some hard to find place that mortals wouldn't think of to look for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-04T20:19:13-07:00","id":1533588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532565-could-you-survive-being-a-vampire?p=1533582#post1533582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not as easy as it sounds; boxes and body-bags can have holes that let light in. You can't be to paranoid enough; if some sunlight gets in, just a little, you could be at final-death before you even woke up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only people who haven't built things with their own hands would have that problem. Sunlight might cause damage to vampires, but it doesn't burn its way through most materials in a time table short of years or decades. A simple pine wood coffin is light tight, if you are worried, then give it a coating of varnish or paint to plug any potential gaps. If you are extra paranoid, then you just use a body bag inside the box. Now someone may want to suggest that vermin might nibble on your body bag or coffin while you are sleeping, but animal instinctively run away from the undead, so that won't be an issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532565-could-you-survive-being-a-vampire?p=1533582#post1533582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Claymores and IEDs are a bad idea; for one, that draws attention of mortals. If you want to wake up one evening with a bunch of firefighters and detectives examining your body, yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, it's almost like a secondary suggestion about a halon system and a locking door was right there in the post to deal with having nosy neighbors.<br /> <br /> Explosives, despite what tv and movies show, generally don't create huge fireballs that create devastation. A relatively small explosive charge inside a contained space can kill a human, hence why you generally don't fire RPGs inside a small room, the back blast of the launcher is enough to damage/kill you. Now that pressure level isn't enough to damage the structure, it just pulps the mortal.<br /> <br /> Contained within a basement, probably being set off mid-day by hunters with all the daytime activity noise going on, the people across the street will hear something, but they won't be able to tell where it came from. Since there is no structural damage as a visual indicator, where are they going to send authorities to if they even bother to call?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532565-could-you-survive-being-a-vampire?p=1533582#post1533582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best way is make a haven mortal-proof is have it in a cemetery or, I took this straight from Ann Rice, is, invest in Potence and get a stone so heavy, no mortal could lift it.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my experience those are some of the worst ways to protect yourself. A cemetery is open to the public during the day, so no one will challenge some strangers wandering about even if they are in groups. Since most cemeteries use modern equipment rather than grave diggers, the sight of someone driving a backhoe around is expected (which means a heavy stone slab is no protection), and last but not least cemeteries tend to be one of the first places people think about when it comes to the undead. So if you are being tracked by hunters, if you always head toward a cemetery before dawn, it's not hard to figure out where you are going.<br /> <br /> Also just for a moment, it is worth considering that despite the size of most modern cemeteries, only a small fraction of the space available will be dedicated to buildings that function as tombs that can be entered and exited. Which means there are relatively few places to look for a place that could hide a vampire who is not using Protean, I say that because once you have protean, you can sleep anywhere there is enough earth to meld with and thus the cemetery is no longer a requirement.<br /> <br /> On the subject of Protean and Potence, even these can be turned against you with a creative hunter. In the case of protean there was a mention of a sabbat pack who slept in an empty lot during the day with earth meld. A camarilla vampire found out where they were sleeping, purchased the lot, and had it paved over during the day. Without the elder variant of earth meld that allows you to swim through the earth, the pack was functionally defeated.<br /> <br /> Likewise with the notion of potence and a heavy stone slab being the answer, this can be turned against you just as easily. Any crypt structure that can hold up a stone slab of that weight will probably be too tough for a vampire to damage. Meaning that all a hunter has to do is weld shut or cement the crypt shut and you have essentially played yourself. According to the strength lifting/breaking chart, depending on the design and materials involved, you would need a combined strength+potence score of 9 or 11 to have a chance at breaking out of that scenario. That is a very heavy investment in both strength and potence, far beyond what a starter vampire with a reasonable character generation would have.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, having several backup havens like a fake crypt at a cemetery is smart, but using that as your primary haven tends to cause more problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-04T20:54:23-07:00","id":1533590,"title":"","content":"Having a couple of back up havens is a given for any smart kindred in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T14:13:27-07:00","id":1533720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532565-could-you-survive-being-a-vampire?p=1533588#post1533588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> . . .<br /> <br /> Hmm, it's almost like a secondary suggestion about a halon system and a locking door was right there in the post to deal with having nosy neighbors.<br /> <br /> Explosives, despite what tv and movies show, generally don't create huge fireballs that create devastation. A relatively small explosive charge inside a contained space can kill a human, hence why you generally don't fire RPGs inside a small room, the back blast of the launcher is enough to damage/kill you. Now that pressure level isn't enough to damage the structure, it just pulps the mortal.<br /> <br /> Contained within a basement, probably being set off mid-day by hunters with all the daytime activity noise going on, the people across the street will hear something, but they won't be able to tell where it came from. Since there is no structural damage as a visual indicator, where are they going to send authorities to if they even bother to call?</div> </div> </div> </div>I live in a city and a compressor blew up with one fatality, everyone was outside looking to see what happened. People are nosy.<br /> <br /> And the odds are, it won't be a lone vampire-hunter that finds your haven, but a kid or twacker; but why risk the mortal-police getting involved?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In my experience those are some of the worst ways to protect yourself. A cemetery is open to the public during the day, so no one will challenge some strangers wandering about even if they are in groups. Since most cemeteries use modern equipment rather than grave diggers, the sight of someone driving a backhoe around is expected (which means a heavy stone slab is no protection), and last but not least cemeteries tend to be one of the first places people think about when it comes to the undead. So if you are being tracked by hunters, if you always head toward a cemetery before dawn, it's not hard to figure out where you are going.<br /> <br /> Also just for a moment, it is worth considering that despite the size of most modern cemeteries, only a small fraction of the space available will be dedicated to buildings that function as tombs that can be entered and exited. Which means there are relatively few places to look for a place that could hide a vampire who is not using Protean, I say that because once you have protean, you can sleep anywhere there is enough earth to meld with and thus the cemetery is no longer a requirement.<br /> <br /> On the subject of Protean and Potence, even these can be turned against you with a creative hunter. In the case of protean there was a mention of a sabbat pack who slept in an empty lot during the day with earth meld. A camarilla vampire found out where they were sleeping, purchased the lot, and had it paved over during the day. Without the elder variant of earth meld that allows you to swim through the earth, the pack was functionally defeated.<br /> <br /> Likewise with the notion of potence and a heavy stone slab being the answer, this can be turned against you just as easily. Any crypt structure that can hold up a stone slab of that weight will probably be too tough for a vampire to damage. Meaning that all a hunter has to do is weld shut or cement the crypt shut and you have essentially played yourself. According to the strength lifting/breaking chart, depending on the design and materials involved, you would need a combined strength+potence score of 9 or 11 to have a chance at breaking out of that scenario. That is a very heavy investment in both strength and potence, far beyond what a starter vampire with a reasonable character generation would have.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, having several backup havens like a fake crypt at a cemetery is smart, but using that as your primary haven tends to cause more problems. </div> </div> </div><br /> Not all cemeteries are open to the public; I inherited one that's abandoned. <br /> <br /> And cement and welding-equipment? Really? How many vampire-hunters carry those with them? To use them, first they'd have to located your haven, and know your location. Why not just stake you with the modern-equipment grave-diggers? <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T14:54:28-07:00","id":1533722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532565-could-you-survive-being-a-vampire?p=1533720#post1533720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I live in a city and a compressor blew up with one fatality, everyone was outside looking to see what happened. People are nosy.<br /> <br /> And the odds are, it won't be a lone vampire-hunter that finds your haven, but a kid or twacker; but why risk the mortal-police getting involved?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending where you live, the locals can be nosy or they can be terrified of getting involved in other peoples business. The WoD setting is supposed to be our world, but worse and more corrupt. IRL there are plenty of examples of people being shot in front of a street full of people and no one saw anything. Now if you are living in some middle to high class suburbs then yeah, the Halon system trap makes more sense than an IED rig, but like I said, the size of the explosive inside a contained area to produce lethal results is remarkably small so their wouldn't be that much sound produced on a comparative level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532565-could-you-survive-being-a-vampire?p=1533720#post1533720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not all cemeteries are open to the public; I inherited one that's abandoned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Private cemeteries are only as private as their security setup, so unless you are paying for maintenance staff to be on site and a security camera system to monitor the place for teenagers, the private vs. public designation is largely pointless. As I previously pointed out, most of the cemetery will consist of graves that can't entered or exited, so the list of places to check goes from a several hour search to 30 minutes or less.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532565-could-you-survive-being-a-vampire?p=1533720#post1533720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And cement and welding-equipment? Really? How many vampire-hunters carry those with them? To use them, first they'd have to located your haven, and know your location. Why not just stake you with the modern-equipment grave-diggers?</div> </div> </div> </div>A credit card and a trip to the local Home Depot pretty much gives any hunter access to most stuff they need other than guns and body armor, what sort of hunters do you run in your games? Seriously, there are way safer ways to do hunting using a hardware store than trying to out gun a vampire and their allies.<br /> <br /> I am confused, are you suggesting that to use cement/welding equipment/backhoe etc. requires you to locate a vampires haven, but using a stack on the vampire while they are asleep for the day doesn't? If you are running a proper cat and mouse game of hunters vs. vampires, then the hunters will track the vampire back to its haven, then do scouting the following day. If they find the location quickly enough they can run down to the local supply depot and get what they need, if not they come back the next day.<br /> <br /> The reason they wouldn't stake the vampire right then and there is because according to your own statement, the mortals couldn't get at the vampire because to the tomb construction. Thus staking/beheading/burning is out of the question, so they switch to containment.<br /> <br /> To be fair I am visualizing the hunters operating closer to John Carpenters <a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0120877/?ref_=nv_sr_srsg_7_tt_3_nm_5_q_john%2520car\" target=\"_blank\">Vampires</a> movie than the Death Dealers in the first <a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0320691/?ref_=nv_sr_srsg_0_tt_8_nm_0_q_underworld\" target=\"_blank\">Underworld</a> movie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T10:34:07-07:00","id":1533756,"title":"","content":"Seeing as you need to be fine with assaulting and killing people in order to exist.......I'm taking the sun option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T17:41:20-07:00","id":1533777,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bzJDimvPW1Y\" target=\"_blank\">Praise the sun!</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T15:10:58-07:00","id":1533857,"title":"","content":"Honestly no as thanks to my narcisting mother I have the bane weak willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-09T04:13:06-07:00","id":1533884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532565-could-you-survive-being-a-vampire?p=1533777#post1533777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bzJDimvPW1Y\" target=\"_blank\">Praise the sun!</a></div> </div> </div> </div>The question don't really matter. Only that this is the right answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T11:12:22-07:00","id":1533983,"title":"","content":"The question should be asked if any of us could truly handle being ageless and not go mad after seeing loved ones die and the world change beyond your recognition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-10T21:19:12-07:00","id":1534010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532565-could-you-survive-being-a-vampire?p=1533983#post1533983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question should be asked if any of us could truly handle being ageless and not go mad after seeing loved ones die and the world change beyond your recognition?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is a matter of perspective. As you get older, the world changes, people die, technology advances. This is the very definition of a normal mortal life. But vast swaths of humans aren't going off the deep end, that requires excessive social media use.<br /> <br /> Yes humans are social creatures and the vampiric requirement to either avoid attachments or move locations every decade or so can be socially limiting, but this is no different than going to a different state or country for a job or long term education. You reset your connection to the local community every decade or so during your life. The first decade you are just a child who doesn't deal with the world, during the teenage years is either awkwardness or know it all behavior, then during the twenties you tend to get a taste of adult life and wish for your earlier years, etc.<br /> <br /> A better question is how many people can survive in a world where fair play is a luxury rather than a default expectation and the concept of killing you is considered to require less paperwork.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-11T14:43:55-07:00","id":1534050,"title":"","content":"Indeed many of us wouldn't like being part of undead society depicted in Vampire The Masquerade where you are dealing with old and nasty beings who see democracy as a fad and murdering pests is considered acceptable<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-11T17:07:33-07:00","id":1534067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532565-could-you-survive-being-a-vampire?p=1534050#post1534050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed many of us wouldn't like being part of undead society depicted in Vampire The Masquerade where you are dealing with old and nasty beings who see democracy as a fad and murdering pests is considered acceptable</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again, it's a matter of perspective.<br /> <br /> Those who are older, have more experience, and been building resources &amp; influence longer have power over those who are younger, less experienced, and have less resources &amp; influence. The world has worked that way more or less from the beginning. Compared to the last ten thousand years of human history, it is a fad to use democracy as a primary governmental style or not to simply kill those that are giving you problems.<br /> <br /> Vampire society is just human society with a depressing aesthetic style. You could argue that the presence of the Beast and the Hunger make it different, but to tell you the truth when I look at the sheer volume of people who are on mood stabilizers, anti-depressants, anti-psychotics, or require therapy for identity issues, vampire society begins to look rather stable and calm by comparison. <br /> <br /> If you sit and talk with military personnel, police officers, or martial arts practitioners (combat rather than sport), there is a certain appreciation for the honesty of a fight. You live or you die, doesn't matter how it happens, who did what, or even if there were greater moral issues at play. All the other stuff is just noise that distracts from the struggle to survive. That kind of clarity on what matters allows one to improvise, adapt and overcome.<br /> <br /> I suppose it boils down to which level of reality most concerns the given individual. Do they care more about their personal feelings regarding a situation or do they care more about the big picture ramifications. For example, murder is wrong because it disrupts society, unless the person who is to be murdered is more disruptive to society by being alive, then the act of murder becomes the lesser evil, and there for acceptable. What everyone really is arguing about is the criteria for who is the most disruptive.<br /> <br /> VtM gives you the fantasy of being free of death, free of entropy, free of getting old, this in turn means you instinctively want to run wild and indulge in everything unlife has to offer. But the setting is setup so that if you step out of line, you get executed rather than being sent to detention. Some people can't handle that kind of increased stakes, but others see it as just an extension of what life already was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-16T07:09:35-07:00","id":1535725,"title":"","content":"I've got a lot of the fixin's for survival -- but what I lack is the willingness to do it. I had three kids rather late in life, so even though I'm very well-established and comfortable at this point, my kids are still all 5 and under. Endangering them by being a vampire is not an option, and I'd have no willingness to be apart from them. <br /> <br /> So I'm pretty sure that I'd just check out into the sunrise at some point early in the process after taking the time to make all the necessary good byes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-07T21:24:54-07:00","id":1536919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532565-could-you-survive-being-a-vampire#post1532565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How hard is it to survive World of Darkness and a newly embrace Vampire? I think it would be pretty hard, the sun is now your death sentence.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not mentioning the facts that if you don't feed regularly (and as a 13th gen vampire, that means pretty much every day,) or if you're frightened, or made angry, you may become an uncontrollable killing machine (frenzy.) Which means that as a 13th gen vampire, you're weak, and can't control your emotions. You can't hold a day job, you have to sever familial connections if you don't want to eat them. Unless you have a rich and connected patron, you're soon, relatively in immortal time, going to be basically a homeless feral animal. Before you descend into being a literal feral animal (wight.) I know some people like to run this game as &quot;Super Heroes With Fangs,&quot; or as &quot;An Outlet To Be A Psychopath Via Sabbat,&quot; but if you play the game as it was intended, being a vampire really, really sucks, pun intended. And most don't survive the first few years. It's descried as a game of personal horror for a reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25666,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","user":"Illuminostro","date":". 06-08-2024, 12:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}